<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">

  <PropertyGroup>
    <TargetFrameworks>netstandard2.0;net10.0</TargetFrameworks>
    <GenerateDocumentationFile>true</GenerateDocumentationFile>
    <!-- Not every public member is documented (e.g., the Windows Settings enum values) -->
    <NoWarn>$(NoWarn);CS1591</NoWarn>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <PropertyGroup>
    <PackageId>NdefLibrary</PackageId>
    <Product>NFC / NDEF Library</Product>
    <Title>NFC / NDEF Library</Title>
    <Description>Easily parse and create standardized NDEF records for NFC tags.

NDEF (NFC Data Exchange Format) messages are used on NFC tags and to send data between two devices. This library provides a set of classes that enable you to easily work with NDEF records, including URI, Text, Smart Poster, Geo, Social, Telephone, SMS, Mailto, LaunchApp, Android Application Record, Windows Settings and Bluetooth handover records.

The library is platform independent and can be used with any NFC API that reads or writes raw NDEF messages (for example the Windows Proximity APIs). Further NDEF record classes with Windows platform integration are available in the NdefLibraryExtension NuGet package (e.g., to use business cards, iCalendar data or images).</Description>
    <PackageTags>nfc ndef proximity smart poster snep near field communication message record launchapp vcard vcf icalendar ical ics bluetooth handover</PackageTags>
    <PackageLicenseExpression>LGPL-3.0-only OR GPL-3.0-only</PackageLicenseExpression>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <Compile Update="Ndef\NdefExceptionMessages.Designer.cs">
      <DesignTime>True</DesignTime>
      <AutoGen>True</AutoGen>
      <DependentUpon>NdefExceptionMessages.resx</DependentUpon>
    </Compile>
  </ItemGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <EmbeddedResource Update="Ndef\NdefExceptionMessages.resx">
      <Generator>PublicResXFileCodeGenerator</Generator>
      <LastGenOutput>NdefExceptionMessages.Designer.cs</LastGenOutput>
    </EmbeddedResource>
  </ItemGroup>

</Project>
